;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 by the user (written by Claude, from the design,
;; the MACRO manual, LLVM's code generator and the guest runs). Why this
;; is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 3 (section 14, item 11): a SYSTEM.SET64 is a quadword
;;   (.BLKQ), element n bit n MOD 32 of longword n DIV 32, as a HUGEINT's;
;;   a constant is a MOVL of each longword, {0, 31, 32, 63} ^X80000001
;;   twice.
;; - A constructor with a variable element is a SET64 only when a constant
;;   element is above 31 (SemanticActions.CheckConstantSetElement, as on
;;   LLVM): {i} is ASHQ i, #1; i .. j is -1 shifted i places (MNEGL #1 on
;;   both longwords, ASHQ) less -2 shifted j places (MNEGL #2, #1), by
;;   BICL2 of each longword, as LLVM's "-1 shl lo" and "-1 lshr (63-hi)";
;;   the constant elements, here 33, BISL2 of the longword holding them.
;;   ASHQ's count is a byte, the low one of i (MACRO 9-10: a positive count
;;   shifts left, one above 64 gives zero).
;; - +, -, * and / are BISL2, BICL2, BICL2 of MCOML and XORL2 on each
;;   longword, in place when the result is the left operand; -a is MCOML
;;   of each; a SET with a SET64 is zero-extended (MOVL, CLRL).
;; - x IN s is FALSE for x outside 0..63, by an unsigned CMPL with 63. BBC
;;   takes any bit of memory, but of a register only 0..31, a larger
;;   position being a reserved operand (MACRO 9.2.3); so for s in a
;;   register pair a constant x tests bit x MOD 32 of register x DIV 32
;;   (40: #8 of R1), and a variable one shifts the pair right x places
;;   (ASHQ of -x) and tests its low bit, BLBC.
;; - INCL and EXCL with a constant are BISL2 or BICL2 of the bit in its
;;   longword (45: ^X00002000 of a+4); with a variable, of ASHQ i, #1 on
;;   both longwords, an i outside 0..63 leaving the set as it was.
;; - = compares the high longwords, then the low; ORD(a) is the HUGEINT of
;;   its bits, a MOVQ (PredeclaredProcedures.CheckOrd).
;; - Set64Out, built by both backends under -O2 and -OC, prints the same
;;   (output.expected) here and on the guest.
; VaxSet64, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
